  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0149_46d22fef9984.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 328px;\" /></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Maltose is a disaccharide which contain D-glucose as a monosaccharide. Thus, Hydrolysis of maltose&nbsp;with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> gives D-&nbsp;glucose.</p>"
